  "question": {
    "text": "In a resonance tube experiment, to determine the speed of sound in air, a pipe of diameter&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is used. The air column in the pipe resonates with a tuning fork of frequency&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>480</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> when the minimum length of the air column is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. Find the speed of sound ( in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;) in the air at room temperature.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "336",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">v</mtext><mrow><mn>4</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">L</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mn>6</mn><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">r</mtext></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mn>8</mn><mn>0</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>⇒&nbsp;</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>480</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>×</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>×</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>r</mi><mo>]</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>336</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
